course: dictionary
lesson: 13672
title: Ingestion: taking things in through the mouth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ingestion means taking food, drink or another substance into your body through your mouth. When you eat a sandwich or drink a glass of water, you are doing ingestion.
explain: In science lessons on digestion, ingestion is the first stage. «First, the food is taken in by ingestion.» After that comes digestion, when the food is broken down, then absorption, when the useful parts pass into the blood, and egestion, when the waste leaves the body.
explain: Ingestion can also be dangerous. «Harmful by ingestion» on a bottle means do not swallow it. «Accidental ingestion of a battery» means someone has swallowed one by mistake, so you must tell an adult at once.
fact: Ingestion means taking food, drink or another substance into the body through the mouth.
fact: Ingestion is the first stage of digestion, and it comes before digestion, absorption and egestion.
fact: «Harmful by ingestion» means the substance is dangerous if you swallow it.
fact: «Accidental ingestion» means swallowing something by mistake, such as a battery or a medicine.
fact: Ingestion is an uncountable noun, so you write «the ingestion of food», not «an ingestion».
exercise: «Ingestion is the first stage of digestion, when food goes into the mouth.» What does ingestion mean? | Looking at food before you eat it | *Taking food or drink into the body through the mouth | Breaking food down into tiny parts | Getting rid of waste from the body
exercise: «The bottle says harmful by ingestion, so never swallow the liquid.» What does harmful by ingestion warn you? | Drinking it will make you stronger | *Swallowing it could hurt you | It must be kept in the fridge | It tastes of fruit and is safe
exercise: In a science lesson, which of these is an example of ingestion? | Sending nutrients into the blood | Passing waste out of the body | *Eating a cheese sandwich | Breaking food down in the stomach
test: «The toddler had accidental ingestion of a button and went to hospital.» What does accidental ingestion mean? | Sewing a button onto a coat | Losing a button in the house | Swallowing something on purpose to test it | *Swallowing something by mistake
test: Which word means taking food into the body through the mouth? | Absorption | Egestion | *Ingestion | Digestion
exam: «The label on the cleaner says harmful by ingestion.» What should you do if you swallow some? | *Tell an adult straight away and get help | Eat something to fill your stomach | Drink water to wash it down and say nothing | Keep it in your mouth to see how it tastes
